Sleethr  posted 04-10-2001 11:03 AM CT (US)      <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Welp...now that we have got a few of the gems for the quest armors. We need to figure out which faction(s) to go with.<BR>I'm suggestion Coldian as a definite and Dragon as a maybe. Oh okay...kill them damn dragons if ya want...some darn nice stuff drops in SkyShrine. Stuff our Alpha Group could do too...right now! :)<P>Here's the discussion I started on the Praetoriate site about it...figured we should all get on the same sheet of music too. I don't really expect much trouble, but wanted to at least let you all debate and maybe get more input too. I can be wrong, just doesn't happen that often! :-P<P>1) Coldain<BR>2) Giant<BR>3) Dragon<P>Quest risk -vs- reward pretty much follows the order. Of the three faction/quests the Coldian faction/quests offer a good reward and the least risk. Killing giants to raise Coldain faction is almost as easy of a desision to make as killing orcs. Killing giants also raises faction with ClawsofVeeshan ( Dragon ).<P>Giants offer real nice quests, but require you to kill dwarves and dragons to raise faction to get the quests. Giant faction also requires you to kill dragons in the "easy" part of the Temple of Veeshan for the quest armors. Going with Giant faction allows you to kill dwarfs in Icewall for the real nice plate armor that they drop. Going with Giant faction also makes hunting in Skyshrine a non-issue. Some real nice stuff drops in Skyshrine too.<P>Dragon offers some real ultra-uber quest armors...a few AC points better then giant, but still real nice. Dragon faction also allows you to use the Wakening Lands port and hunt in Cobalt Scar without having extra wyverns of cobalt drakes aggro on you. Does make Western Wastes a tad more difficult to hunt in as you can't kill the dragons there, but there is plenty else to kill for exp and loot there.<P>I suggest that a direction is picked now. It really stinks to have half of your guild on one faction and the other half on another. Really limits the things either side can/will hunt together.<P>Myself, I'm thinking Coldain & Dragon is the way to go. Just makes Skyshrine out of limits for hunting. Reason I think coldain/dragon is the way to go is for both short term and long term.<P>Short Term: Killing Giants to get coldain quest armor is something a small guild can do. 1-2 group raids on giant town can outfit the guild with the coldain quest armor fairly easily. 1-2 group raids can get everything except for maybe the chest. I think you need to kill the giant king for quest chest armor drops, but could be wrong. <P>Long Term: Using the Coldain quest armors, you can then work on the Dragon quest armors as the guild power develops.<P>Easy Loot Greed Problem: /drool The darn dorfs and Skyshrine mobs drop some darn good armors and weapons. Just a few stats short of Hate/Fear gear for the melee types.<P>Part II:<BR>Did some comparision "shopping" with the quest armors...all armors have the same spell effects per peice. Some effects are rather nice. All of the armors would be nice to have. Some peices are better then others for a particlar class. Druid bracer stats and effect is rather nice, while all the other priest class bracers pretty much stink stat wise. <P>Looking at pure stat values. In order of best stats to lowest.<BR>1) Dragon<BR>2) Giant<BR>3) Coldain<P>AC bing one of the few stats that really matter...in order of best to worst.<BR>1) Giant<BR>2) Dragon<BR>3) Coldain<P>In order of most obtainable to least:<BR>1) Coldain<BR>2) Giant<BR>3) Dragon<P>Dragon Faction Reality Check time...<P>A show of hands for who where will regularly if ever kill 65th lvl dragons in the Testing Hall ( deep inside ) of the Temple of Veeshan.<P>Unless we all join Divine or some other uber-guild...I don't see any hands coming up for this poll.<P>So..I want Dragon Faction so I can port into Wakening Lands without Woushi killing me.<P>Cobalt Scar portal is an excellent alternative. Yes...there are agro Cobalt Drakes that path close, but you can survive them if not inviso. Buff cold resists. Zone to Skyshrine is very close to CS Port Circle and Zone to Wakening Lands is very close to SS/CS zone point.<P>Based on reality ( as I see it ) and greed for the nice drops in Skyshrine. Verser is going for Coldain and killing giants and dragons. They are all evil and must be stopped. Sleethr will probably still try and get good coldain and dragon faction though, but not going to stress out over the dragon faction stuff like I used to.<P>As a guild, Division 13 will go with Coldain faction. Giants will be fair game and Dragons will still be open for debate.<P>Comments everyone?<P> <BR>Nefarius   posted 04-10-2001 11:21 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Well I've been killing giants on and off for 15 levels now, and I don't see that changing. I've been trying to hit anything with positive dragon faction I can see just so I can hopefully use the WL port someday. And Cura, no more pissing off he farie(Tunare) thingies in WL. Thats one faction I don't want to lose yet. <BR>Lonar   posted 04-10-2001 12:03 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Well, good luck with the Coldain quests. :) They are definetely the easy way out for now, but I think you should consider a few other things before jumping into your faction commitments.<BR>1. Thurgadin is pretty "out of the way", and you don't ever need to go there if you don't want to. So becoming KOS to them is no great loss.<BR>2. You will have to go through kael unless you port to WL or CS.<BR>3. AC is king. Giant armor has the best AC. All other stats are pretty much moot in my eyes.<BR>4. Getting quest armor drops inside Kael for Coldain quests is not a good risk vs. reward scenario if you ask me. High risk for the lowest questable armor.<BR>5. Dwarfs just BEG to be slaughtered. :)<BR>6. By going with "dragon" faction you limit yourselves to NOT killing most of the mobs with great loot drops. Maybe you can't kill them now, but someday you will. And that day will come LONG before you do any of the quests they give out.<P>These are just the opinions and ramblings of a twisted little gnome. Take Care all. :)<P>Sendil<BR>44th Level Suicide Rogue of Blood Tide<BR>Lonar Baardeth<BR>53rd Level Gnecromancer of Blood Tide<BR>Solusek Ro Server <P> <BR>Sleethr   posted 04-10-2001 12:26 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>IF Div 13 was a big guild or aligned with an uber guild like Afterlife ( Giant Faction ). Going after Giant faction by killing Dorfs and Dragons would be the way I would want to go also. Based on all the reasons you listed. That dropped dorf armor is sooo darn nice.<BR>But..seeing how the Coldain quests are at least possible to do with a 1-2 group raid...I don't see a good reason for us to go with giant faction.<P>Mainly...we just aren't a Giant Quest Faction/Planes/Trak capable guild and never will be.<P> <BR>Lonar   posted 04-10-2001 12:38 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>I could be wrong here, since I've gone with Giant faction. But in order to get drops off the giants for the coldain quests, you are gonna need more than 1-2 groups to get in there and get it. If your 1-2 groups average about 55th level, then its probably doable, but much lower than that and you are just begging for lots of CR.<BR>Sendil / Lonar<BR> <BR>Ghall   posted 04-10-2001 01:54 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>That's what we're talking about Lonar 2 groups of mid 50's peeps taking on the giants. Any non-claws faction aligned Giant has the capicity to drop the armor we need. We just need to camp the middle and see how far we can move in.<BR>We will NEVER be big enough to take ToV. Just not enough players or enough accounts/time in the day.<BR> <BR>Nefarius   posted 04-10-2001 02:00 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>And beyond any other point, these giant geeks are trying to muscle in on my gods turf. And I just ain't having that. <BR>Foggy   posted 04-10-2001 02:20 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Dorf lover! <BR>Sleethr   posted 04-10-2001 02:29 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Now we just need Foggy to see the light and start killing giants with us.<BR>You check with your guild about what factions they are going for yet Foggy? Kinda hurts to not have people to hunt with in those zones. Seeing how 95% of the adventures in those quest zone are guild only, pickup groups really aren't an option either. <BR> <BR>Lonar   posted 04-10-2001 03:07 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Ghall, last time I checked Div 13 didn’t have one group of mid-50s, let alone 2. :) If you plan to take down giants in and near the castle area this is what I would take with me:<BR>2 Warriors<BR>2 Rogues<BR>2 Clerics<BR>2 Enchanters<BR>2 Shaman/Bard/Druid<BR>2 other melees would be nice, but just about anyone will do<P>with an *average* level of 55. Chanters will hopefully be 57+, as most velious mobs, at the level these giants are, are pretty darn hard to keep under control. Basically what I’m saying is, it’s doable with 2 groups but *I* sure wouldn’t want to try it. :) Also, keep in mind the difficulty of pulling corpses out of cities in Velious. A necro to summon corpses may become an absolute necessity if you have a total wipeout. I’m not trying to discourage you from killing the giants, just playing devils advocate and telling you what I’ve seen personally.<P>Here is something else to consider. If you take 2 groups with an average level of around 52-53, you can kill everything in Skyshrine up to and including the “maze”. You can go in even further than that if you’ve got some really good or higher level enchanters/meleers. Maybe it’s the “loot whore” in me coming out… but I’d much prefer to lay waste to nearly an entire zone with relative ease and get a good 6-8 awesome drops, then spend hours hoping for one piece of quest armor to drop in a very unstable/unsafe environment. If you haven’t looked at any of the drop tables in Skyshrine they are pretty darn nice. Besides, who doesn’t enjoy killing dwarfs? &#61514; <P>Anyway, feel free to ignore all this, its merely my observations and opinions based on the things I’ve seen and done in Velious. Take a look around your server, and others, and see where most folks are aligning themselves… it isn’t Thurgadin. BUT, looking at it from that standpoint, you’ll have less competition to do the dorf quests. /shrug Oh well.<P>Just the ramblings of a silly old gnome.<P>Sendil / Lonar<P> <BR>tenlaar   posted 04-10-2001 09:38 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Cura says Amen on killin dwarfs<BR> <BR>Ghall   posted 04-11-2001 07:49 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Right now we do not .. you are correct, but we DO have 2 FULL groups of people that WILL eventually get to 55th level. We won't be UBER but we will be 2 groups strong.  <BR>Ghall   posted 04-11-2001 07:54 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Even if we could take ALL of skyshrine none of the giant quest stuff drops there. We wont be able to clear Icewell, or ToV or Sirens Grotto or Velks Lab or any other REALLY bitchen zone either.<BR>It's just the way veRANT wants the game to work for non uber people.<BR> <BR>Sleethr   posted 04-11-2001 08:53 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Well...with 2 balanced groups...we could do those zones at 50-60th.<BR>Most of those 50+ zones have un-mezzable mobs, so having a melee heavy group and just 1 chanter to buff and mezz the ones they could would be enough. 2 Clerics would be good. <P>Thinking too far ahead now. :)<P>Just having more 45+ folks would make me happy. I'm sure we could come up with some nice areas to hunt making do with what we have. We have become pretty darn good at coming up with solutions to problems that do without enchanters, do without clerics and even without warriors. :)<P> <BR>Lonar   posted 04-11-2001 09:50 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>I think you're missing my point Ghall. To hell with doing ANY of the quests. If you can get enough people to spend enough time praying for a few quest related drops, and if you aren't concerned with having the "uber" quest items, why even *bother* with the quests? Just take those same people and go camp for some gear. It'll take *far* less time, far less effort, and far less frustration to see some results. <BR>You may think that just because I'm in Blood Tide I can go and do whatever I feel like, but BT isn't really bothering with the quest armor in Velious. We have done Plane of Growth for a good portion of our "uber" armor, and if we come across some quest items we think, "Cool, maybe we'll get the other parts some other day." We are NOT wasting our time at the moment working on these quests, as the payoff is not really worth the effort right now. We are concentrating on getting everyone 50+ in the guild their hate/fear gear, then going after the big mobs in Kunark, once those are trivial, and we get some BP drops from Trakanon, then we will possibly concentrate on some of these quests. But that’s a little ways off in the future. <P>Oh, just a little something for the bards here... Last night we cleared Hate again trying to get the last drop for a mage epic, (didn’t get it, second night in a row), and we had Bard arms, breastplate, helm, legs, and a bracer drop. The armor drops in Hate are incredible these days, I’d highly recommend that anyone who is planes capable, and has armor drops in hate, to try like hell to get up there. We must have had a good 20-30 armor drops in just one clearing of hate, add that to the clearing on Monday night, and we have added around 50-60 new pieces of planar gear to our members. Fear on the other hand seems to be just as stingy as it used to be. I think the last time we did a full clearing of fear we got maybe 10-12armor drops. We only saw 4 boogeymen (drops necro stuff), and got a pair of blighted trousers. The druids ended up with the most drops by virtue of there being about 12 gorgons. Damn druids.<P>Anyway, I’m rambling again, and got WAY off track. These are only my opinions, and as you are well aware, trying to type what I mean is more difficult than talking. :) so give me a call sometime you putz! Rich has my number.<P>Sendil / Lonar<P> <BR>Sleethr   posted 04-11-2001 11:02 AM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>1) Did some killing in SS with Verser last night.<BR>Screw dragon faction!<P>2) Looked at some of the Giant quests.<P>Hmmm...I kill some 49th lvl dorf and take what he drops to some giant and get some +8WIS/INT Boots ALL/ALL or some nice +WIS/INT Gloves? <P>Wonder if it's too late for Sleethr to switch factions? :)
